		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=374#comment-2135</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[Jemaluddin (Mark) was a great gift to us in Va. I danced and sang with him uncounted times over the years. We often ended the Kalama at the same wondrous note staring into the beauty of the group and the spirit. 
At Joshua Tree, he taught and watched us grow.
At camps his guitar and voice were like stars in the night.
One night we sang with our teacher &quot;My heart is Rainin&#039; Stars, and time stopped for a while.
As he weakened, we talked at times, or emailed, and felt the pain that comes to those of us who know from Medicine that we are so very mortal. 
I had the deep honor of singing with and for  him at his ceremony in the woods as we buried him- his favorite song -My Life Goes on in Endless Song.
To him goes much love and blessing, as he was a blessing to us. May we all remember and emulate his love and compassion, and go on in endless song...]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Jemaluddin (Mark) was a great gift to us in Va. I danced and sang with him uncounted times over the years. We often ended the Kalama at the same wondrous note staring into the beauty of the group and the spirit.<br />
At Joshua Tree, he taught and watched us grow.<br />
At camps his guitar and voice were like stars in the night.<br />
One night we sang with our teacher &#8220;My heart is Rainin&#8217; Stars, and time stopped for a while.<br />
As he weakened, we talked at times, or emailed, and felt the pain that comes to those of us who know from Medicine that we are so very mortal.<br />
I had the deep honor of singing with and for  him at his ceremony in the woods as we buried him- his favorite song -My Life Goes on in Endless Song.<br />
To him goes much love and blessing, as he was a blessing to us. May we all remember and emulate his love and compassion, and go on in endless song&#8230;</p>
]]></content:encoded>
